DESCRIPTION:MIAMI BEACH BUSINESS READY DAYS Thursday\, February 19 | 9AM 
 – 2PM City Hall (1700 Convention Center Drive\, City Hall Building Dep
 artment – 2nd Floor Conference Room) The City of Miami Beach will host
  a Business-Ready Day on Thursday\, February 19 \, from 9 a.m. to 2 p.m.
  at City Hall (1700 Convention Center Drive\, City Hall Building Departm
 ent – 2nd Floor Conference Room) . Business Ready Days are held quarte
 rly and are designed to serve as a one-stop resource for local entrepren
 eurs and business owners. During the event\, businesses can receive pers
 onalized assistance with obtaining or renewing their Business Tax Receip
 t (BTR)\, along with guidance on City and County regulatory requirements
 . Representatives from all departments involved in the BTR process will 
 be available to provide coordinated\, in-person support. Participating C
 ity of Miami Beach departments include Planning and Zoning\, Building\, 
 Finance\, Fire\, Economic Development\, Procurement\, Tourism and Cultur
 e\, Public Works\, and the Office of Emergency Management. County partne
 rs include the Miami-Dade County Building Department\, Department of Reg
 ulatory and Economic Resources (DERM)\, Water and Sewer Department\, and
  the Miami-Dade County Tax Collector’s Office. Together\, these agenci
 es will help businesses better understand permitting\, compliance\, and 
 operational requirements. The Economic Development Department will be av
 ailable to discuss business incentive programs\, site selection assistan
 ce\, and the City’s Business Concierge Service\, which supports busine
 sses navigating City processes and accessing local resources. The Public
  Works Department will provide guidance on the Sidewalk Café Program\, 
 including application requirements and best practices for activating out
 door dining spaces. The Procurement Department will offer guidance on ve
 ndor certification and local government contracting opportunities\, whil
 e the Office of Emergency Management will share information on the Busin
 ess Emergency Response Team (BERT) program. Partner organizations will a
 lso participate\, including BrightStar Credit Union\, which will be on s
 ite to share information about its business banking products\, financial
  programs\, funding opportunities\, and small business resources.\nSourc
 e and updates: https://events.miamibeachfl.gov/event/miami-beach-busines
